#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:1
msgid "CheckAbort and Progress events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:3
msgid "What is CheckAbort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:5
msgid ""
"VTK filter execution can take a while, so being able to abort a running "
"filter is very important. Aborting is done using "
"`vtkAlgorithm::SetAbortExecute(on)`. However, as the algorithm is computing "
"when we want to abort it, this is usually called from another thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:9
msgid ""
"Within the algorithm, `vtkAlgorithm::CheckAbort` can be used to check that "
"flag and setup the pipeline for aborting the algorithm. It is used like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:11
msgid ""
"for (vtkIdType i = 0; !this->CheckAbort() && i < bigNumber; i++)\n"
"{\n"
"  // Long operation\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:18
msgid ""
"This is fine for non-distributed filters, but is not recommended for "
"application working in distributed, because it requires calling "
"`SetAbortExecute` on each rank at the exact same \"step\" in the algorithm; "
"distributed algorithms need all ranks to abort at the same time to avoid "
"deadlocks. This is not feasible in practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:22
msgid ""
"See [this issue](https://gitlab.kitware.com/vtk/vtk/-/work_items/18463) for "
"more context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:24
msgid ""
"While `CheckAbort` is not deprecated, it is not recommended. Use "
"`CheckAbortAndInvoke` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:26
msgid "What is CheckAbortAndInvoke"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:28
msgid ""
"As its name indicates, `CheckAbortAndInvoke` merely calls CheckAbort and "
"then invoke a `CheckAbort` event. An event can be observed by other class to "
"execute code when invoked. This lets applications using VTK observe this "
"event and react accordingly, usually it means synchronising the state of "
"`AbortExecute` flag accross distributed ranks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:33
msgid ""
"However this also implies that calling `CheckAbortAndInvoke` will trigger "
"inter process communication, which can be very expensive. Such event should "
"be invoked infrequently and deliberately. Calling it on every loop iteration "
"would create a lot of overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:36
msgid "What are Progress Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:38
msgid ""
"Progress Events are events invoked by vtkAlgorithm to signal processing "
"progress of the algorithm, with a double progressing from 0.0 to 1.0 . "
"Applications using VTK can observe this event to show a progress bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:41
msgid ""
"Progress events are invoked regularly but only a few times, because they can "
"imply communication between a client and a server, similarly as "
"CheckAbortAndInvoke. Moreover, applications using VTK may rely on that "
"progress event to update the abort status using SetAbortExecute when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:44
msgid ""
"This makes progress events and abort checks very similar; ParaView takes "
"advantage of progress events to check for aborts. See [this discourse post]"
"(https://discourse.paraview.org/t/paraview-client-server-communication-and-"
"abort-support/17430/3) for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:47
msgid "Implementation examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:49
msgid "Simple case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:51
msgid ""
"Here is a simple example of a progress and abort check implementation in a "
"filter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:53
msgid ""
"vtkIdType numCells = ds->GetNumberOfCells();\n"
"if (numCells == 0)\n"
"{\n"
"  return true;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// This harcoded value can vary depending on the complexity of the "
"algorithm.\n"
"// The point is to avoid calling CheckAbort too fast even with small "
"datasets\n"
"vtkIdType minCheckAbort = 1000;\n"
"\n"
"// We iterate on the cells, so we will check abort and update progress 10 "
"times during computation\n"
"vtkIdType checkAbortInterval = std::min(numCells / 10 + 1, minCheckAbort);\n"
"\n"
"for (vtkIdType i = 0; i < numCells; i++)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (i % checkAbortInterval == 0)\n"
"  {\n"
"    this->UpdateProgress(static_cast<double>(i) / numCells);\n"
"    if (this->CheckAbortAndInvoke())\n"
"    {\n"
"      break;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"  }\n"
"  // <Data processing>\n"
"}\n"
"return true;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:83
msgid "Multi step case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:85
msgid ""
"Often, algorithms are split in multiple parts, so we can split the progress "
"using `SetProgressShiftScale`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:87
msgid ""
"vtkIdType numCells = ds->GetNumberOfCells();\n"
"if (numCells == 0)\n"
"{\n"
"  return true;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"vtkIdType minCheckAbort = 1000;\n"
"vtkIdType checkAbortInterval = std::min(numCells / 10 + 1, minCheckAbort);\n"
"bool abort = false;\n"
"\n"
"this->SetProgressShiftScale(0, 0.3) // Progress will move from 0.0 to 0.3\n"
"for (vtkIdType i = 0; !abort && i < numCells; i++)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (i % checkAbortInterval == 0)\n"
"  {\n"
"    this->UpdateProgress(static_cast<double>(i) / numCells);\n"
"    if (this->CheckAbortAndInvoke())\n"
"    {\n"
"      abort = true;\n"
"      break;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"  }\n"
"  // Some short operations\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"if (abort)\n"
"{\n"
"  return true; // Aborting is not a failure case\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"this->UpdateProgress(1.0); // Not absolutely needed but in some case it may "
"be useful to ensure the threshold is actually reached\n"
"\n"
"if (this->CheckAbortAndInvoke()) // Ok to check anytime\n"
"{\n"
"  return true;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"this->SetProgressShiftScale(0.3, 0.7) // Progress will move from 0.3 to 1.0\n"
"for (vtkIdType i = 0; i < numCells; i++)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (i % checkAbortInterval == 0)\n"
"  {\n"
"    this->UpdateProgress(static_cast<double>(i) / numCells);\n"
"    if (this->CheckAbortAndInvoke())\n"
"    {\n"
"      break;\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"  // Some long operations\n"
"}\n"
"return true;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:142
msgid "Multithreaded case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:144
msgid ""
"VTK Algorithms often multi-thread their critical loops. Here is how to abort "
"during a multi-threaded worker execution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:146
msgid ""
"void operator()(vtkIdType begin, vtkIdType end)\n"
"{\n"
"  const bool isFirst = vtkSMPTools::GetSingleThread();\n"
"  constexpr vtkIdType minCheckAbortInterval = 1'000'000; // "
"minCheckAbortInterval can go pretty high if the algorithm is fast\n"
"  vtkIdType checkAbortInterval = std::min(this->NumberOfCells / 10 + 1, "
"minCheckAbortInterval);\n"
"  for (vtkIdType cellId = begin; cellId < end; ++cellId) // There is no "
"insurance that begin and end will progress over time, but thats the best we "
"got\n"
"  {\n"
"    if (isFirst && cellId % checkAbortInterval == 0) // Only the first "
"thread should check\n"
"    {\n"
"      this->Self->UpdateProgress(static_cast<double>(cellId) / this-"
">NumberOfCells); // The progress may be a bit erratic but generally it "
"works\n"
"      if (this->Self->CheckAbortAndInvoke())\n"
"      {\n"
"        break;\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"    else if (this->Self->GetAbortOutput()) // All threads should abort\n"
"    {\n"
"      break;\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"[...]\n"
"\n"
"MyWorker worker;\n"
"worker();\n"
"return 1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:178
msgid "Internal filter case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:180
msgid ""
"Algorithm often use internal filters, that use their own CheckAbortAndInvoke "
"and progress event, which should be forwarded to the main filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/CheckAbort.md:182
msgid ""
"namespace\n"
"{\n"
"void OnAbortCheckCallback(\n"
"  vtkObject* caller, unsigned long vtkNotUsed(eid), void* clientData, void* "
"vtkNotUsed(callData))\n"
"{\n"
"  vtkAlgorithm* internalAlgorithm = static_cast<vtkAlgorithm*>(caller);\n"
"  vtkMyFilter* self = static_cast<vtkMyFilter*>(clientData);\n"
"\n"
"  if (self->CheckAbortAndInvoke())\n"
"  {\n"
"    internalAlgorithm->AbortExecuteOn();\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"vtkMyFilter::vtkMyFilter()\n"
"{\n"
"  vtkNew<vtkEventForwarderCommand> forwarder;\n"
"  forwarder->SetTarget(this)\n"
"  this->InternalAlgorithm->AddObserver(vtkCommand::ProgressEvent, "
"forwarder);\n"
"\n"
"  this->InternalAbortCheckCallbackCommand-"
">SetCallback(::OnAbortCheckCallback);\n"
"  this->InternalAbortCheckCallbackCommand->SetClientData(this);\n"
"  this->IntenalAlgorithm->AddObserver(\n"
"    vtkCommand::AbortCheckEvent, this->InternalAbortCheckCallbackCommand);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"[...]\n"
"\n"
"int vtkMyFilter::RequestData(\n"
"  vtkInformation* request, vtkInformationVector** inputVector, "
"vtkInformationVector* outputVector)\n"
"{\n"
"  // Make sure all filters are not aborted at this point\n"
"  this->InternalAlgorithm->AbortExecuteOff();\n"
"\n"
"  // Execute internal filter\n"
"  return this->InternalAlgorithm->ProcessRequest(request, inputVector, "
"outputVector);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
